  "rationale": "Every entry foothold is reachable, so workstation:execution, memoryDump:credentialAccess, browserStore:credentialAccess and configSecret:credentialAccess are all reachable. Each has at least two independent ways in (for example, browserStore can be reached directly from supplychain). The target is an OR over several collection steps. One route is jumpHost (via browserStore or memoryDump) to shareMount to the target. A second route is fileServer (via memoryDump or dbLogin) to vaultRead to the target. Blocking shareMount or jumpHost leaves the vaultRead route open. Blocking fileServer or vaultRead leaves the shareMount route open. Blocking memoryDump leaves jumpHost (via browserStore) and fileServer (via dbLogin) available. Blocking browserStore leaves jumpHost and fileServer both reachable via memoryDump. Blocking workstation leaves dbLogin unreachable, but fileServer and jumpHost are still reachable via memoryDump. No other single step lies on every route to the target, so no step is a single point of failure."
